@startuml
!theme plain
autonumber
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam shadowing false

<style>
sequenceDiagram {
  participant {
    BackgroundColor #E0F2F1
    BorderColor #00796B
  }
}
</style>

title **Food Rescue Platform (Replate) - Driver Dispatch, Live Telemetry & Routing**

actor "Volunteer Driver\n(Mobile / Web App)" as Driver
participant "Driver Dashboard / Hook" as App
participant "Dispatch Router" as Dispatch
participant "OSRM Routing Engine" as OSRM
database "PostgreSQL / Vehicles" as DB
participant "WebSocket Server" as WS
actor "Donor / NGO Clients" as Watchers

== 1. Driver Availability & Location Stream ==
Driver -> App: Toggle Duty "On Duty"
App -> Dispatch: POST /drivers/me/availability { status: 'AVAILABLE', location: {lat, lng} }
activate Dispatch
Dispatch -> DB: UPDATE vehicles SET availability_status='AVAILABLE', current_location='POINT(lng, lat)'
Dispatch --> App: 200 OK (Driver is Online)
deactivate Dispatch

loop Every 10-30 Seconds (Live Telemetry Ping)
  App -> Dispatch: POST /drivers/me/location { latitude, longitude }
  activate Dispatch
  Dispatch -> DB: UPDATE vehicles SET current_location='POINT(lng, lat)'
  Dispatch -> WS: Broadcast driver position update
  WS --> Watchers: Push updated driver coordinate
  Dispatch --> App: 200 OK
  deactivate Dispatch
end

== 2. Automated Dispatch Allocation ==
note over Dispatch: Triggered when NGO accepts a donation offer
Dispatch -> DB: SELECT * FROM vehicles WHERE availability_status='AVAILABLE' AND capacity_kg >= donation.quantity
DB --> Dispatch: Available Candidate Vehicles
Dispatch -> Dispatch: Sort candidates by haversine_distance(vehicle.current_location, pickup_location)
Dispatch -> DB: Assign best candidate:\nINSERT INTO deliveries (status='DRIVER_ASSIGNED', driver_id, donation_id, ngo_id)\nUPDATE vehicles SET availability_status='BUSY'
Dispatch -> WS: Push notification to matched driver
WS --> App: "New Delivery Assigned: Pickup from Donor X"

== 3. Turn-by-Turn Route Navigation & Live ETA ==
Driver -> App: Click "Accept Delivery"
App -> Dispatch: GET /drivers/me/job
activate Dispatch
Dispatch -> DB: SELECT active delivery + pickup & dropoff coordinates
DB --> Dispatch: Delivery, Pickup {lat, lng}, Dropoff {lat, lng}

Dispatch -> OSRM: GET /route/v1/driving/{driver_lng},{driver_lat};{pickup_lng},{pickup_lat}
OSRM --> Dispatch: GeoJSON Route Polyline, Distance (meters), Duration (seconds)

Dispatch --> App: DriverJob JSON (Stops, Route Polyline, ETA)
deactivate Dispatch

App -> App: Render Leaflet Route Map & Turn-by-Turn Path
App -> WS: Stream live progress along polyline
WS --> Watchers: Donor & NGO track live driver icon moving towards pickup

== 4. Handling Driver Issue / Exception ==
alt Breakdown or Vehicle Issue
  Driver -> App: Click "Report Issue" (e.g. Flat Tyre, Breakdown)
  App -> Dispatch: POST /deliveries/{id}/report-issue { reason, details }
  activate Dispatch
  Dispatch -> DB: UPDATE deliveries SET status='DRIVER_ISSUE'
  Dispatch -> DB: UPDATE donation SET status='DRIVER_ISSUE'
  Dispatch -> DB: UPDATE vehicles SET availability_status='OFFLINE'
  Dispatch -> WS: Broadcast Alert to Operations & Admin
  Dispatch -> Dispatch: Trigger Auto-Reassignment to next closest driver
  Dispatch --> App: 200 OK (Dispatched assistance / re-assigned)
  deactivate Dispatch
end

@enduml
